  "name": "Coord runners (admin)",
  "description": "Per-runner drain, restart readiness and session wind-down (/admin/coord/runners), plan 2026-09-13-drained-runner-never-reaches-idle Phase 8. ci-bot is a superuser so the page renders its real content. The page reads its device from `?device=` (run-spec-ci.ts seeds the sentinel below) and makes four reads: GET /api/v1/operations/fleet/health (the DevicePicker roster), GET /fleet/drain (the drain badge + DeviceDrainControl), GET /fleet/resource-samples?device_id=&history=false (the readiness verdict riding the device's newest resource sample) and GET /sessions/fleet?device_id= (the session census). metadata.routeStubs fulfills all four so the populated states render deterministically: one fresh, unsafe readiness sample whose wind_down_sessions name two sessions (an idle operator-terminal session and a busy steward), matched by claude_code_session_id to two census rows. The stubs are load-bearing: without them the sentinel device has no sample and no sessions, and the populated state goes red. AUTHORED FROM SOURCE, NOT DERIVED: no dev stack or authed UI Bridge snapshot was available in the authoring session, so every criterion below is an authored data-testid read off page.tsx and verified by page.specSelectors.test.tsx against a jsdom render, not against a live capture. Re-derive from a live authed snapshot when one is available (console style guide §6.3). Read-only; structural only.",
